-- title:
--   Hecke coordinates mod 2^m on the inertia part of T₂J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $B$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ lying over $2$, in the sense that $2$ belongs to the non-units of $B$; the Hecke algebra $\mathtt{HeckeAlg}=\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,\mathbb{P}\,\mathbb{Z}$ acts on $J_0(p)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ through `heckeModuleBar p`. Write $L$ for the subgroup of sequences $x:\mathbb N\to J_0(p)$ satisfying $2^n\cdot x_n=0$ and $2\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$ for all $n$ (the $2$-adic Tate module) whose every component lies in the subgroup generated by the displacements $\sigma\cdot x-x$ with $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $B$ over $\mathbf Q$ (the image of $B$'s inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbf Q}(\overline{\mathbf Q})$) and $x$ killed by some power of the Eisenstein maximal ideal at $2$. Let $\mathbb T=$ `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅`, the image of the weight-$2$ level-$p$ Hecke algebra (no excluded primes) in $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Z}$ of the integral lattice in $S_2(\Gamma_0(p))$. The assertion: there are $C\in\mathbb N$ and additive maps $\Phi_m:L\to\mathbb T/(2^m)$ such that (i) whenever $t\in\mathbb T$ reduces mod $2^{m+1}$ to $\Phi_{m+1}(s)$, it reduces mod $2^m$ to $\Phi_m(s)$; (ii) $\Phi_m(t\cdot s)=\overline{t}\,\Phi_m(s)$ for $t\in\mathtt{HeckeAlg}$ acting componentwise and preserving $L$, where $\overline{t}$ is the image of $t$ under `heckeEvalForms p 2` followed by restriction to the lattice, reduced mod $2^m$; and (iii) $\#\bigl(\ker\Phi_m/(2^mL\cap\ker\Phi_m)\bigr)\le 2^C$ for every $m$.
--
--   This provides a tower of rank-one Hecke-equivariant coordinates, with a uniform defect bound, on the inertia-displacement part of the $2$-adic Tate module of $J_0(p)$, in the style of Mazur's analysis of the Eisenstein ideal. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_addMonoidHom_torsionBy_two_pow_inf_closure_inertia_smul_sub_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_natCard_ker_le_of_multiplicativeTypeNat`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_addMonoidHom_torsionBy_two_pow_inf_closure_inertia_smul_sub_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_natCard_ker_le_of_multiplicativeTypeNat).
